":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/deployments","created_at":"2017-02-01T10:48:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T03:05:54Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-05T00:20:37Z","git_url":"git://github.com/open5gs/open5gs.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:open5gs/open5gs.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs","homepage":"https://open5gs.org","size":88373,"stargazers_count":2803,"watchers_count":2803,"language":"C","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1152,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":348,"license":{"key":"agpl-3.0","name":"GNU Affero General Public License v3.0","spdx_id":"AGPL-3.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/agpl-3.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["3gpp","4g","5g","5gc","core","epc","lte","network","nr","open5gs"],"visibility":"public","forks":1152,"open_issues":348,"watchers":2803,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Open5GS Release, Revision, or Tag\n\nv2.7.7\n\nThe issue was reproduced in a controlled test environment with:\n\n```text\nUPF PFCP endpoint: 127.0.0.7:8805\nUPF GTP-U endpoint: 127.0.0.7:2152\nPFCP CP endpoint:  127.0.0.5:8805\n\nglobal.max.ue: 1024\n```\n\nThe tested UPF was built with ASan enabled, but the process termination is caused by an explicit Open5GS assertion (`ogs_abort()`), not by an ASan memory-safety finding.\n\nThe relevant GTP-U Error Indication path contains:\n\n```c\n/* src/upf/gtp-path.c */\n\nif (report.type.error_indication_report) {\n    ogs_assert(far->sess);\n    sess = UPF_SESS(far->sess);\n    ogs_assert(sess);\n\n    ogs_assert(OGS_OK ==\n        upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request(sess, &report));\n}\n```\n\n`upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request()` creates a local PFCP transaction and returns `OGS_ERROR` if the transaction cannot be allocated:\n\n```c\nxact = ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create(\n        sess->pfcp_node, sess_timeout, OGS_UINT_TO_POINTER(sess->id));\n\nif (!xact) {\n    ogs_error(\"ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create() failed\");\n    return OGS_ERROR;\n}\n```\n\nTherefore, when PFCP transaction/timer resources are exhausted, the allocation failure is propagated as `OGS_ERROR`, but the caller converts it into a fatal assertion.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start the UPF from a clean state.\n\n2. Establish a PFCP association with the UPF.\n\n3. Establish one PFCP session containing a PDR associated with a FAR whose Outer Header Creation uses:\n\n```text\nRemote GTP-U TEID: 0x11111111\nRemote GTP-U IPv4: 127.0.0.9\n```\n\nThe session used in this reproduction had:\n\n```text\nUE IPv4:      10.45.0.2\nIngress TEID: 0x00000044\nFAR ID:       1\nPDR ID:       1\n```\n\n4. Keep the PFCP association alive normally.\n\nPFCP Heartbeat Requests are answered normally.\n\n5. Continuously receive and drain PFCP Session Report Requests (`message type 56`) sent by the UPF, but deliberately do **not** send PFCP Session Report Responses.\n\nThis keeps the generated Session Report transactions outstanding while preventing the receiver's UDP socket buffer from becoming the limiting factor.\n\n6. Send valid GTP-U Error Indication messages to:\n\n```text\n127.0.0.7:2152\n```\n\nThe Error Indication contains:\n\n```text\nTEID Data I:\n    TEID = 0x11111111\n\nGTP-U Peer Address:\n    IPv4 = 127.0.0.9\n```\n\nThe complete GTP-U packet used for the reproduction is:\n\n```text\n321a0010000000000001000010111111118500047f000009\n```\n\n7. Send 6000 copies using batches of 20 packets with a 10 ms delay after each batch:\n\n```python\nfor sent in range(1, 6001):\n    sock.sendto(error_indication, (\"127.0.0.7\", 2152))\n\n    if sent % 20 == 0:\n        time.sleep(0.01)\n```\n\nNo process-liveness checks or subprocesses are executed during the sending loop.\n\nIn the reproduced run:\n\n```text\nPFCP session established: 17:46:47.829\nUPF abort:                17:46:50.632\n```\n\nThe crash therefore occurred approximately 2.8 seconds after session establishment.\n\nWith the test configuration above (`global.max.ue=1024`), approximately 5.5k outstanding Error-Indication-triggered reports were sufficient to exhaust the timer pool.\n\nThe exact threshold is configuration- and timing-dependent. The 6000-packet count is used here for reproducibility and should not be interpreted as a universal threshold.\n\n\n\n### Logs\n\n```text\n09/16 17:46:50.632: [event] ERROR: Failed to allocate timer object from pool (../lib/core/ogs-timer.c:84)\n09/16 17:46:50.632: [pfcp] ERROR: Maximum number of xact->tm_delayed_commit[16384] reached (../lib/pfcp/xact.c:119)\n09/16 17:46:50.632: [upf] ERROR: ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create() failed (../src/upf/pfcp-path.c:371)\n09/16 17:46:50.632: [upf] FATAL: _gtpv1_u_recv_cb: Assertion `OGS_OK == upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request(sess, &report)' failed. (../src/upf/gtp-path.c:367)\n09/16 17:46:50.633: [core] FATAL: backtrace() returned 9 addresses (../lib/core/ogs-abort.c:37)\n\n/path/to/open5gs/build_v2.7.7/src/upf/../../lib/core/libogscore.so.2(ogs_abort+0xcd)\nopen5gs-upfd(+0xa6632)\nlibogscore.so.2(+0x139136)\nopen5gs-upfd(+0x7b205)\nlibogscore.so.2(+0xdee44)\nlibasan.so.8(+0x5ea42)\nlibc.so.6(+0x9cb84)\nlibc.so.6(+0x129ecc)\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe UPF should remain alive when PFCP transaction or timer resources are exhausted.\n\nA failure of `ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create()` while processing a GTP-U Error Indication should be handled as a recoverable allocation/resource-exhaustion condition.\n\nFor example, the UPF could:\n\n* log the failed Session Report allocation;\n* drop additional reports once resources are exhausted;\n* coalesce repeated Error Indications for the same FAR/session;\n* rate-limit Error-Indication-triggered Session Reports;\n* limit the number of outstanding Session Report transactions;\n* return from the GTP-U receive callback without aborting the process.\n\nIn particular, an `OGS_ERROR` returned by `upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request()` should not terminate the whole `open5gs-upfd` process through `ogs_assert()`.\n\n\n\n### Observed Behaviour\n\nEach matching GTP-U Error Indication causes the UPF to generate a PFCP Session Report Request.\n\nBecause the Session Report Responses are not returned in this reproduction, the local PFCP transactions remain outstanding and accumulate.\n\nEach PFCP transaction requires timer objects. With:\n\n```text\nglobal.max.ue = 1024\ntimer pool    = 16384\n```\n\nthe timer pool is eventually exhausted.\n\n`ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create()` then fails and returns `NULL`.\n\n`upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request()` correctly propagates this as `OGS_ERROR`, but `_gtpv1_u_recv_cb()` contains:\n\n```c\nogs_assert(OGS_OK ==\n    upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request(sess, &report));\n```\n\nThis converts the allocation failure into a fatal process-wide abort.\n\nThe failure sequence is therefore:\n\n```text\nRepeated valid GTP-U Error Indications\n        ↓\nPFCP Session Report Requests are generated\n        ↓\nLocal PFCP transactions remain outstanding\n        ↓\nPFCP transaction/timer resources accumulate\n        ↓\nglobal timer pool is exhausted\n        ↓\nogs_pfcp_xact_local_create() returns NULL\n        ↓\nupf_pfcp_send_session_report_request() returns OGS_ERROR\n        ↓\n_gtpv1_u_recv_cb() reaches the fatal assertion\n        ↓\nopen5gs-upfd aborts\n```\n\n\n### Relation to potential duplicates\n\nGitHub suggested #4491, #4791 and #4699 as potential duplicates.\n\nThis issue is different from #4491, which concerns malformed GTP-U traffic causing a SIGSEGV in the GTP-U packet parsing/rule-matching path.\n\nIt is also different from #4699, which is triggered by a stateful PFCP sequence involving malformed Outer Header Creation fields and terminates with `Unknown family(0)`.\n\n#4791 is related because it also involves PFCP transaction/timer pool exhaustion. However, #4791 exhausts **remote PFCP transactions** through direct PFCP traffic on UDP/8805 and crashes in `ogs_pfcp_xact_receive()` after `ogs_pfcp_xact_remote_create()` fails.\n\nThe issue reported here is triggered through **GTP-U Error Indications on UDP/2152**, causes accumulation of **local PFCP Session Report transactions** created by `ogs_pfcp_xact_local_create()`, and terminates in `_gtpv1_u_recv_cb()` when `upf_pfcp_send_session_report_request()` returns `OGS_ERROR`.\n\n\n\n### eNodeB/gNodeB\n\n_No response_\n\n### UE Models and versions\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/4792/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31816946223,"node_id":"LE_lADOBM4HkM8AAAABNp-AJc8AAAAHaHASLw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/events/31816946223","actor":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_u